dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.prim.lambda.closure]/4: the closure type's function call
operator has the lambda's compound-statement as its body.  The front end
type-checks that body in place when the lambda-expression is encountered
but did not mark it converted, so the end-of-unit sweep that completes
half-converted SYSTEM-HEADER bodies (cpp_typecheckt::typecheck) converted
it a second time; the re-check of `return mv(o.r_)' saw the call's xvalue
result as an lvalue ("invalid implicit conversion from 'pair &' to
'pair &&'") and the lambda's body was dropped.  This is libc++ 18's
basic_string(basic_string &&) (<string> line 925): the moved-to string was
nondet under libc++ (KNOWNBUG libcxx_string_move_ctor_lambda, cvise
reduction /tmp/r163/red).  Fixed in round 163b.  The #line directive
places the class in a system header; user code was unaffected.
